<div><b>1. Fundamentals of Sociology (PA-113)</b><br></div>
<div><br></div>
<div><b>Topics:</b><br></div>
<div>	•	<b>Definition of Sociology</b>:</div>
<div>	•	Focus on its relationship with other social sciences.</div>
<div>	•	Study examples of how sociology impacts public administration and policymaking.</div>
<div>	•	<b>Socialization</b>:</div>
<div>	•	Learn various agents (family, school, media, peers).</div>
<div>	•	Review Cognitive Development Theory (Piaget’s stages of development).</div>
<div>	•	<b>Why Important</b>:</div>
<div>	•	Connect sociology to policymaking, social issues, and modern challenges.</div>
<div><br></div>
<div><b>Study Approach:</b><br></div>
<div>	1.	<b>Conceptual Understanding</b>:</div>
<div>	•	Use books like <i>Introduction to Sociology</i> and online articles to understand definitions and relationships.</div>
<div>	2.	<b>Examples</b>:</div>
<div>	•	Think of real-life cases (e.g., public policies based on social studies).</div>
<div>	3.	<b>Practice Questions</b>:</div>
<div>	•	Write short notes on agents of socialization and cognitive development.</div>
