<div><b>2. Fundamentals of Economics (PA-112)</b><br></div>
<div><br></div>
<div><b>Topics:</b><br></div>
<div>	•	<b>Microeconomics vs. Macroeconomics</b>:</div>
<div>	•	Understand definitions, differences, and how both are used in public administration.</div>
<div>	•	<b>Production Possibility Frontier (PPF)</b>:</div>
<div>	•	Graphical representation, opportunity cost, unattainable points, and efficiency.</div>
<div>	•	<b>Demand and Elasticity</b>:</div>
<div>	•	Draw demand curves from data.</div>
<div>	•	Learn the formula for price elasticity and factors affecting the demand curve.</div>
<div><br></div>
<div><b>Study Approach:</b><br></div>
<div>	1.	<b>Graphs and Calculations</b>:</div>
<div>	•	Practice drawing PPF curves and demand graphs with hypothetical data.</div>
<div>	2.	<b>Numerical Practice</b>:</div>
<div>	•	Solve examples of elasticity calculations (like the ones in your paper).</div>
<div>	3.	<b>Understand Policies</b>:</div>
<div>	•	Think of policies where economic principles (demand, supply) apply.</div>
<div><br></div>
<div><b>3. Introduction to Public Administration (PA-111)</b><br></div>
<div><br></div>
<div><b>Topics:</b><br></div>
<div>	•	<b>Definition and Approaches</b>:</div>
<div>	•	Study definitions and approaches (scientific, behavioral, etc.).</div>
<div>	•	<b>Scientific Management</b>:</div>
<div>	•	Review Frederick W. Taylor’s principles and their applications.</div>
<div>	•	<b>Max Weber’s Bureaucratic Model</b>:</div>
<div>	•	Understand key features like hierarchy and formal rules.</div>
<div>	•	<b>Henri Fayol’s Scalar Chain</b>:</div>
<div>	•	Understand how this relates to coordination and communication.</div>
<div><br></div>
<div><b>Study Approach:</b><br></div>
<div>	1.	<b>Diagrams</b>:</div>
<div>	•	Create visual diagrams of Weber’s bureaucratic model and Fayol’s scalar chain.</div>
<div>	2.	<b>Examples</b>:</div>
<div>	•	Use examples from Bangladesh’s public administration system.</div>
<div>	3.	<b>Compare Theories</b>:</div>
<div>	•	Compare Taylor, Weber, and Fayol for better understanding.</div>
<div><br></div>
